data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc` with `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work as expected:

```csharp
Span<nint> signedSpan = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> unsignedSpan = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

No `unsafe` context is needed (thanks to `Span<T>`). On this 64-bit system, each `nint`/`nuint` is 8 bytes. The only caveat is that `sizeof(nint)` requires `unsafe` since the size isn't fixed at compile time — use `nint.Size` instead.
